This target generates images that can be used on ARM machines with EFI
support (e.g EDKII/TianoCore or U-Boot with bootefi).

Tested:
THTF ChaoXiang TF830-V050

Kernel selection
----------------
Linux 6.18 is the default. Enable CONFIG_TESTING_KERNEL to build Linux 5.10.
Both versions use the same device profiles and image formats:

  armv8:     Generic EFI, ext4 and squashfs combined images
  e2000:     E2000Q/D Demo and MiniITX, squashfs factory/sysupgrade images
  phytiumpi: FireFly 2 GB and 4 GB, ext4 factory/sysupgrade images

armv8 EFI includes the out-of-tree D3000M DC, GPU, VPU and NPU packages
(kmod-phytium-dc/gpu/vpu/npu). Their original sources and compatibility
patches are kept in package/kernel/phytium-d3000m. The FTD330 DC driver is
separate from the older in-tree Phytium display driver used by other boards.

PhytiumPi uses kmod-rtw88-8821cs and its firmware for the onboard RTL8821CS.
The wireless stack is supplied by the mac80211 packages on both kernels.

Select the subtarget and devices with make menuconfig, run make defconfig,
then make -j30. If a build fails, use make -j1 V=s to diagnose the failure.
For multiple devices, use CONFIG_TARGET_MULTI_PROFILE and the corresponding
CONFIG_TARGET_DEVICE_phytium_<subtarget>_DEVICE_<device> selections.

E2000 and PhytiumPi partition layout
----------------------------------
The kernel partition is now 12 MiB, since the new kernels exceed the old
6 MiB partition. E2000 rootfs starts at 15424 KiB in a factory image and
12352 KiB in a sysupgrade image. PhytiumPi rootfs starts at 16 MiB in a
factory image. The E2000 DTB partition remains 64 KiB.

Install a full factory image when migrating from the old 6 MiB layout.
Normal sysupgrade requires an existing kernel partition of at least 12 MiB.
The compatibility version is 2.0. EFI disk images keep their existing layout.

The image builder updates the saved U-Boot environment and its CRC in a
build-time copy of the firmware. The bundled firmware binaries are unchanged.
Kernel size checks reject images that exceed the reserved kernel partition;
recovery initramfs images are separate and do not have this flash-size limit.

Linux 6.18 platform sources
--------------------------
The board device trees are retained from the 5.10 target. Peripheral drivers
use Phytium Embedded SDK v3.4 (d50081ae7d93bf124be6722f14fb5c96600e7621)
where available, with Linux 6.18 API adaptations. Phytium GEM clock control
and firmware matching extend the upstream macb driver; newer GMAC devices
use the separate phytmac driver.
